  "kind": "excel-differs-from-math",
  "title": "WEIBULL and WEIBULL.DIST return 0 for PDF at x = 0 and use double-rounded x87 powers diverging up to 4.2 ULP",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 and 16.0.20527, WEIBULL and WEIBULL.DIST return 0 at x = 0 even in PDF mode (cumulative = FALSE) and even when alpha <= 1, after checking that beta^alpha neither overflows (#NUM!) nor underflows to 0 or a subnormal (#DIV/0!). For x > 0, Excel evaluates r = RN53(RN64(x/beta)) and raw x87 exp(RN53(RN64(alpha*ln(r)))) powers, returning -expm1(-t) for CDF or left-to-right double-rounded (alpha/beta^alpha)*x^(alpha-1)*exp(-t) for PDF, differing up to 4.2 ULP from the true mathematical CDF/PDF. WEIBULL.DIST returns #NAME? in compatibility version 1.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Recorded in crates/calc-func/witness-reference/WEIBULL.DIST.tsv (Excel 16.0.20131) and prefix_metadata (rows 241-242, Excel 16.0.20527.20088), and matched across 2,951/2,952 WEIBULL and 31,481/31,483 WEIBULL.DIST full-bank rows plus 120/120 pinned WEIBULL.DIST rows.",
